OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Notifications/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the app targets
list `Sources` + `TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,misc-surfaces,
shared-surfaces}` — there is no `TeslaSync/Features`). The repo's real, compiled canonical page
home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/**`, which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml
source path (createIntermediateGroups). The sibling P7 `page:notifications/AuditLog` ships there
(`Sources/Features/Notifications/NotificationsAuditLog*.swift`) and recorded the identical
reconciliation. This page therefore ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Notifications/**`, the
faithful equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Notifications`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This is the only deviation from
the literal prompt path; the gate placeholder scan + xcodegen + full xcodebuild were all re-pointed
at the real path and run green (below).

TYPE-NAME SWEEP: `ChannelsPage` / `ChannelsPageModel` / `ChannelsPageSampleData` /
`ChannelsRouteRegistration` are all collision-free across Sources + TeslaSync + Tests (0 prior
declarations). The single prior `notificationsChannels` token is the breadcrumb string key
`routes.notificationsChannels` (LayoutBreadcrumbs.Routes.swift L99), not an AppRoute case — no clash.

PARITY SCOPE: the web `ChannelsPage` is a thin wrapper — `<PageContainer title subtitle copyLink>`
framing `<NotificationChannelsView />` (the channels CRUD surface that lives at its own route so it
gets a real page title/breadcrumb instead of being a tab). The manifest record for THIS unit declares
zero panels / zero charts / zero maps / zero data sources / zero data-states and exactly 2 strings —
so the parity scope is the wrapper itself. The embedded `NotificationChannelsView` is a SEPARATE,
already-shipped parity unit (`TeslaSync/feature-views/NotificationChannelsView*.swift`, P4 0188); this
page composes it, it does not re-implement it. The native wrapper reproduces the web 1:1 using the
shared native `PageContainer` shared-surface (the parity of the web `PageContainer`, incl. the
copy-link affordance) embedding the existing `NotificationChannelsView`. The embedded view owns its
own loading / empty / error / data + live-freshness states, so the page never renders a blank region.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route `/notifications/channels` is nested (App.tsx). A dedicated
`.notificationsChannels` AppRoute case is added (pathSegment `notifications/channels` → `.path`
`/notifications/channels` matching web exactly; Operations group alongside `.notifications` +
`.notificationsAudit`; icon `bell.badge.fill`), `AppRouteParser` aliases `/notifications/channels`
→ `.notificationsChannels` (required — the generic first-segment fallback would otherwise resolve
`.notifications`), and `ChannelsRouteRegistration` hosts the page, chained into `\.routeHosts` in
TeslaSyncApp.swift right after `NotificationsAuditLogRouteRegistration`. The Explore feature-hub
catalog derives from `AppRoute.allCases`, so the new route is auto-covered (ExploreCatalogTests count
invariant stays green). Every RouteTests invariant (unique path segments, group membership) holds and
`/notifications` still resolves to `.notifications` (no regression) — all executed below.

